WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.932 --> 00:00:02.726
- It was very difficult
for me to figure out

00:00:02.726 --> 00:00:04.609
where my boundaries were,

00:00:04.609 --> 00:00:07.944
Because I'd grown up poor
and didn't have anything.

00:00:07.944 --> 00:00:11.376
I can't quit this job because this is what

00:00:11.376 --> 00:00:12.940
everybody else wants to do,

00:00:12.940 --> 00:00:16.252
and if I quit this job,
what am I going to do.

00:00:16.252 --> 00:00:18.898
What we all want is to be able to live out

00:00:18.898 --> 00:00:22.565
the truest, highest
expression of ourselves.

00:00:24.804 --> 00:00:28.871
When people show you who
they are, believe them

00:00:28.871 --> 00:00:30.121
the first time.

00:00:31.409 --> 00:00:33.324
- Hello Believe Nation, it's Evan.

00:00:33.324 --> 00:00:35.861
My one word is believe
and I believe in people

00:00:35.861 --> 00:00:37.709
more than they believe in themselves

00:00:37.709 --> 00:00:39.355
and my sincere hope is that

00:00:39.355 --> 00:00:41.951
if you see in yourself what I see in you,

00:00:41.951 --> 00:00:43.767
you'll be able to change the planet.

00:00:43.767 --> 00:00:45.555
So to help you in your journey today,

00:00:45.555 --> 00:00:47.262
we're going to learn from entrepreneur,

00:00:47.262 --> 00:00:49.537
talk show host and
philanthropist, Oprah Winfrey

00:00:49.537 --> 00:00:53.759
and my take on her top 10 rules
for success, volume three.

00:00:53.759 --> 00:00:55.401
Rule number six is my personal favorite

00:00:55.401 --> 00:00:57.702
and I'd love to know which
one you guys like the best.

00:00:57.702 --> 00:00:59.551
Also as you're watching,
if you hear something

00:00:59.551 --> 00:01:01.014
that really resonates with you,

00:01:01.014 --> 00:01:02.865
please leave it down in the comments below

00:01:02.865 --> 00:01:04.328
and put quotes around it so other people

00:01:04.328 --> 00:01:05.669
can be inspired by it as well.

00:01:05.669 --> 00:01:07.637
And if you leave it in
the first couple of hours

00:01:07.637 --> 00:01:08.974
of this video going live,

00:01:08.974 --> 00:01:13.057
you have a chance to win
one of two daily prizes.

00:01:15.231 --> 00:01:17.731
(grand music)

00:01:24.930 --> 00:01:26.289
- You know, because when I
first started making money

00:01:26.289 --> 00:01:30.291
and it was, you know, my
salary or my earnings,

00:01:30.291 --> 00:01:33.590
were published all over the place.

00:01:33.590 --> 00:01:35.596
I mean, the first year I was like really?

00:01:35.596 --> 00:01:38.846
Did I make that much money, oh, my God.

00:01:39.765 --> 00:01:41.347
It was very difficult for me to figure out

00:01:41.347 --> 00:01:45.676
where my boundaries were
because I'd grown up

00:01:45.676 --> 00:01:47.772
poor and didn't have anything.

00:01:47.772 --> 00:01:49.519
So it's easy when you don't have anything

00:01:49.519 --> 00:01:50.914
and people ask you for money.

00:01:50.914 --> 00:01:52.811
They say I need 500 and
you say I don't have it,

00:01:52.811 --> 00:01:56.478
because I'm just trying
to get my rent paid.

00:01:57.641 --> 00:02:00.504
It's harder when you're
multi-billion dollar

00:02:00.504 --> 00:02:02.964
salary is now in the paper
and you get a lot of friends

00:02:02.964 --> 00:02:05.881
and cousins you didn't have before.

00:02:07.070 --> 00:02:10.121
So, how do you set
boundaries for yourself?

00:02:10.121 --> 00:02:12.170
I was having trouble setting
boundaries for myself

00:02:12.170 --> 00:02:13.753
for even strangers.

00:02:14.997 --> 00:02:16.843
People would just show
up at my door in Chicago

00:02:16.843 --> 00:02:19.870
and say Oprah, I left my
husband, please help me

00:02:19.870 --> 00:02:23.449
and I would because she knows I have it.

00:02:23.449 --> 00:02:26.532
So, don't try that now, though, okay?

00:02:29.928 --> 00:02:30.926
Don't try that now.

00:02:30.926 --> 00:02:32.343
I figured it out.

00:02:34.514 --> 00:02:37.973
So what I learned was is
that oh, the reason why

00:02:37.973 --> 00:02:40.313
people keep showing up
is because my intention

00:02:40.313 --> 00:02:42.954
is to make them think that
I'm such a nice person

00:02:42.954 --> 00:02:46.425
that you can ask me for anything.

00:02:46.425 --> 00:02:48.863
You can get me to do anything.

00:02:48.863 --> 00:02:50.650
I'm going to say yes,
I'm going to say yes.

00:02:50.650 --> 00:02:53.943
So when Stevie called me this time,

00:02:53.943 --> 00:02:57.579
I thought I'd try out
my first no on Stevie.

00:02:57.579 --> 00:02:59.407
Let's start big.

00:02:59.407 --> 00:03:01.542
He wanted me to donate
some money to a charity

00:03:01.542 --> 00:03:03.718
and I didn't want to donate to the charity

00:03:03.718 --> 00:03:06.925
because I have my own charities

00:03:06.925 --> 00:03:08.595
and I care about a lot of people,

00:03:08.595 --> 00:03:10.766
but the problem is when you have money,

00:03:10.766 --> 00:03:13.059
everybody thinks you just
want to give to everything.

00:03:13.059 --> 00:03:14.768
So, every letter I ever get starts with

00:03:14.768 --> 00:03:17.268
we know you love the children.

00:03:19.525 --> 00:03:20.907
Yes, I do love the children,

00:03:20.907 --> 00:03:24.765
but somebody else is going
to have to help the children.

00:03:24.765 --> 00:03:28.808
So I said to Stevie, I said to Stevie, no.

00:03:28.808 --> 00:03:33.097
And as a person who has
that disease to please,

00:03:33.097 --> 00:03:36.894
I was waiting for him
then to say I will never

00:03:36.894 --> 00:03:40.670
speak to you again, I will never call you,

00:03:40.670 --> 00:03:43.420
I will never sing a song for you.

00:03:44.329 --> 00:03:45.329
And he didn't.

00:03:45.329 --> 00:03:47.314
He just said, okay.

00:03:47.314 --> 00:03:48.147
Okay?

00:03:49.347 --> 00:03:50.791
Okay, it's okay?

00:03:50.791 --> 00:03:53.374
He said, okay, check you later.

00:03:56.498 --> 00:03:58.877
What I learned from that is many times

00:03:58.877 --> 00:04:02.431
you will have angst and worry about things

00:04:02.431 --> 00:04:06.761
and put yourself in a state,
like someone said this morning,

00:04:06.761 --> 00:04:07.939
because they're phone went off,

00:04:07.939 --> 00:04:10.151
they were mortified over
a phone I said, really?

00:04:10.151 --> 00:04:12.676
You will put yourself in a state

00:04:12.676 --> 00:04:16.983
when the other person really
isn't even thinking about you.

00:04:16.983 --> 00:04:20.983
So, learning that I could
specifically determine

00:04:22.567 --> 00:04:26.150
for myself what the
boundaries were for me,

00:04:27.101 --> 00:04:31.872
what I wanted to do, give
my money, give my time,

00:04:31.872 --> 00:04:35.429
give of my service to who
I wanted to give it to

00:04:35.429 --> 00:04:38.009
when I did, that I get
to make that a decision

00:04:38.009 --> 00:04:41.052
and just because you
get 100 requests a week

00:04:41.052 --> 00:04:44.751
doesn't mean you have to
try to fulfill all of that.

00:04:44.751 --> 00:04:48.597
Just because you have all of
these demands on your time

00:04:48.597 --> 00:04:52.680
and on you doesn't mean
that you have to say yes.

00:04:53.514 --> 00:04:57.189
You get to decide because
you're the master of your fate,

00:04:57.189 --> 00:04:59.378
the captain of your soul as

00:04:59.378 --> 00:05:01.519
William Ernest Henley said in Invictus.

00:05:01.519 --> 00:05:04.119
And understanding that really changed

00:05:04.119 --> 00:05:07.504
the meaning of my life in that I was not

00:05:07.504 --> 00:05:11.671
no longer drive by what
other people wanted me to do,

00:05:12.589 --> 00:05:15.422
but took charge of my own destiny,

00:05:16.351 --> 00:05:18.883
making choices based upon what do I feel

00:05:18.883 --> 00:05:21.383
is the next right move for me.

00:05:23.742 --> 00:05:26.794
Quincy Jones had, I would not
even say an important role,

00:05:26.794 --> 00:05:29.453
I would say the role in my acting career.

00:05:29.453 --> 00:05:32.822
Quincy Jones discovered me
and it's so interesting to me

00:05:32.822 --> 00:05:36.129
because when I was working
as a television newswoman

00:05:36.129 --> 00:05:39.025
in Baltimore and really all I wanted to do

00:05:39.025 --> 00:05:41.314
was be an actress, but
I was doing television

00:05:41.314 --> 00:05:45.481
and I felt at the time,
well, I can't quit this job

00:05:46.844 --> 00:05:49.888
because this is what
everybody else wants to do

00:05:49.888 --> 00:05:53.451
and if I quit this job,
what am I going to do?

00:05:53.451 --> 00:05:57.044
And I was going to a
speech coach at the time

00:05:57.044 --> 00:05:58.791
that the station had sent me to.

00:05:58.791 --> 00:06:01.737
The broadcasting school,
they send everybody

00:06:01.737 --> 00:06:03.992
to the same woman, and I
was telling her, you know,

00:06:03.992 --> 00:06:05.072
I really don't want to do this.

00:06:05.072 --> 00:06:06.576
What I really want to do is act.

00:06:06.576 --> 00:06:08.503
And she said my dear,
you don't want to act

00:06:08.503 --> 00:06:10.523
because if you wanted to
act, you'd be doing it.

00:06:10.523 --> 00:06:12.565
What you want to be, my dear, is a star.

00:06:12.565 --> 00:06:15.002
Because if you wanted
to act you'd be waiting

00:06:15.002 --> 00:06:16.447
tables in New York.

00:06:16.447 --> 00:06:17.681
And I thought, now why
am I going to work tables

00:06:17.681 --> 00:06:19.271
if I'm already working in TV?

00:06:19.271 --> 00:06:22.285
So, I said, well, what I
think is going to happen

00:06:22.285 --> 00:06:25.873
is I will be discovered
because I want it so badly,

00:06:25.873 --> 00:06:28.130
somebody's going to have to discover me.

00:06:28.130 --> 00:06:29.633
And she said you just dream.

00:06:29.633 --> 00:06:30.997
You're a dreamer.

00:06:30.997 --> 00:06:33.290
So when it happened, I called her up.

00:06:33.290 --> 00:06:36.198
I said you will not believe this.

00:06:36.198 --> 00:06:37.920
I got discovered.

00:06:37.920 --> 00:06:39.444
And it really was a discovery.

00:06:39.444 --> 00:06:40.970
It's like one of those
Lana Turner stories,

00:06:40.970 --> 00:06:43.246
only it wasn't a drugstore.

00:06:43.246 --> 00:06:46.050
He was in his hotel room, saw me on TV.

00:06:46.050 --> 00:06:47.332
It was unbelievable.

00:06:47.332 --> 00:06:52.002
The interesting thing
about that is that I truly

00:06:52.002 --> 00:06:55.835
believe that thoughts
are the greatest vehicle

00:06:57.062 --> 00:07:01.201
to change power and success in the world.

00:07:01.201 --> 00:07:02.855
Everything begins with thoughts.

00:07:02.855 --> 00:07:04.521
I mean the chairs that we're sitting in,

00:07:04.521 --> 00:07:06.264
the room that we're in all started because

00:07:06.264 --> 00:07:08.643
somebody thought it.

00:07:08.643 --> 00:07:12.400
So, I thought up the
Color Purple for myself.

00:07:12.400 --> 00:07:14.250
I know this is going to
sound strange to you,

00:07:14.250 --> 00:07:18.314
I read the book, I got so
many copies of that book.

00:07:18.314 --> 00:07:20.748
I passed the book around
to everybody I knew.

00:07:20.748 --> 00:07:23.881
If I was on the bus, I'd
pass it out to people.

00:07:23.881 --> 00:07:26.883
And when I heard that there
was going to be a movie,

00:07:26.883 --> 00:07:29.488
I started talking it up for myself.

00:07:29.488 --> 00:07:32.071
I didn't know Quincy
Jones or Steven Spielberg

00:07:32.071 --> 00:07:34.672
or how on earth I would get in this movie.

00:07:34.672 --> 00:07:36.135
I'd never acted in my life.

00:07:36.135 --> 00:07:39.386
But I felt it so intensely that I had

00:07:39.386 --> 00:07:40.582
to be a part of that movie.

00:07:40.582 --> 00:07:43.449
I just, I really do believe
I created it for myself.

00:07:43.449 --> 00:07:46.144
I wanted it more than
anything in the world

00:07:46.144 --> 00:07:48.080
and would have done anything to do it.

00:07:48.080 --> 00:07:50.032
Anything to do it.

00:07:50.032 --> 00:07:52.449
Turn your wounds into wisdom.

00:07:53.405 --> 00:07:55.640
You will be wounded
many times in your life.

00:07:55.640 --> 00:07:57.180
You'll make mistakes.

00:07:57.180 --> 00:07:59.108
Some people will call them failures,

00:07:59.108 --> 00:08:02.385
but I have learned that
failure is really God's way

00:08:02.385 --> 00:08:06.747
of saying excuse me, you're
moving in the wrong direction.

00:08:06.747 --> 00:08:08.358
It's just an experience.

00:08:08.358 --> 00:08:11.858
(applauding and cheering)

00:08:13.312 --> 00:08:16.562
Just an experience, just an experience.

00:08:17.629 --> 00:08:20.141
I remember being taken
off the air in Baltimore,

00:08:20.141 --> 00:08:24.201
being told that I was no
longer being fit for television

00:08:24.201 --> 00:08:26.275
and that I could not anchor the news

00:08:26.275 --> 00:08:27.718
because I used to go out on the stories

00:08:27.718 --> 00:08:31.131
and my own truth was, even
though I'm not a weeper,

00:08:31.131 --> 00:08:35.295
I would cry for the people in the stories,

00:08:35.295 --> 00:08:37.093
which really wasn't very
effective as a news reporter

00:08:37.093 --> 00:08:39.760
to be covering a fire and crying

00:08:41.151 --> 00:08:44.889
because the people lost their house.

00:08:44.889 --> 00:08:48.722
And it wasn't until I
was demoted as an on-air

00:08:50.211 --> 00:08:53.585
anchorwoman and thrown
into the talk show arena

00:08:53.585 --> 00:08:56.795
to get rid of me that
I allowed my own truth

00:08:56.795 --> 00:08:58.746
to come through and the
first day I was on the air

00:08:58.746 --> 00:09:01.689
doing my first talk show back in 1978,

00:09:01.689 --> 00:09:04.310
it felt like breathing, which is what

00:09:04.310 --> 00:09:06.397
your true passion should feel like.

00:09:06.397 --> 00:09:09.636
It should be so natural to you

00:09:09.636 --> 00:09:11.749
and so I took what had been a mistake,

00:09:11.749 --> 00:09:15.749
what had been perceived as
a failure with my career

00:09:15.749 --> 00:09:17.694
as an anchorwoman in the news business

00:09:17.694 --> 00:09:19.771
and turned it into a talk show career

00:09:19.771 --> 00:09:22.572
that's done okay for me.

00:09:22.572 --> 00:09:24.259
- What drives you to keep working so hard?

00:09:24.259 --> 00:09:27.732
You could, you know, you and
I are in the 60s category

00:09:27.732 --> 00:09:29.727
and so when you're 60s, you've lived more

00:09:29.727 --> 00:09:31.250
than you're going to live.

00:09:31.250 --> 00:09:32.246
- Yeah.

00:09:32.246 --> 00:09:33.750
- Realistically, so when
you realize you've lived

00:09:33.750 --> 00:09:35.172
more than you're going to
live, you can say why not

00:09:35.172 --> 00:09:36.617
relax a little bit, why not just ease up,

00:09:36.617 --> 00:09:38.585
why have you decided to work even harder

00:09:38.585 --> 00:09:40.031
than you did before?

00:09:40.031 --> 00:09:42.202
- Because it think, David, that everybody,

00:09:42.202 --> 00:09:44.338
you know the thing that worked for me

00:09:44.338 --> 00:09:47.304
all these years whether
it was the magazine

00:09:47.304 --> 00:09:52.033
or, which I still have, or
whether it was the show,

00:09:52.033 --> 00:09:54.756
I understood that there's
a common denominator

00:09:54.756 --> 00:09:57.399
in the human experience
and I want the same thing

00:09:57.399 --> 00:10:00.348
you want, which is the same
thing you want and you want.

00:10:00.348 --> 00:10:03.437
What we all want is to be able to live out

00:10:03.437 --> 00:10:07.020
the truest, highest
expression of ourselves

00:10:08.351 --> 00:10:10.403
as a human being.

00:10:10.403 --> 00:10:13.148
That doesn't end until
you take your last breath.

00:10:13.148 --> 00:10:16.272
What is the truest, highest vision

00:10:16.272 --> 00:10:17.960
that you hold for yourself?

00:10:17.960 --> 00:10:19.545
No matter where you are in your life,

00:10:19.545 --> 00:10:21.655
there's always the next level.

00:10:21.655 --> 00:10:23.810
There's always the next
level till the last breath.

00:10:23.810 --> 00:10:27.347
So I feel that I always
knew that I would be done

00:10:27.347 --> 00:10:30.174
with the show when I
felt like oh, I've said

00:10:30.174 --> 00:10:33.604
as much as I could say
here on this platform

00:10:33.604 --> 00:10:35.718
and then how will I be used?

00:10:35.718 --> 00:10:38.298
If there were a theme song to my life,

00:10:38.298 --> 00:10:40.008
Amazing Grace would be one of them

00:10:40.008 --> 00:10:42.321
and Keep On Using Me Till You Use Me Up

00:10:42.321 --> 00:10:43.357
would be another one.

00:10:43.357 --> 00:10:45.105
(laughing)

00:10:45.105 --> 00:10:46.347
You know that Bill Withers song.

00:10:46.347 --> 00:10:48.518
Da, da, da, da, da, da, da, da, da.

00:10:48.518 --> 00:10:52.926
So I feel that until
you have used your value

00:10:52.926 --> 00:10:54.433
as a human being, you're not done.

00:10:54.433 --> 00:10:57.818
When I first started as
a broadcaster, I was 19,

00:10:57.818 --> 00:10:59.977
very insecure, thrown into television,

00:10:59.977 --> 00:11:04.308
pretending to be Barbara
Walters, looking nothing like her

00:11:04.308 --> 00:11:07.210
and still going to college.

00:11:07.210 --> 00:11:08.777
So I do all my classes in the morning

00:11:08.777 --> 00:11:11.639
from 8 to 1 and then the
afternoon I work from 2 to 10

00:11:11.639 --> 00:11:13.751
and did the 6:00 news.

00:11:13.751 --> 00:11:17.026
And would stay up and
study and all that stuff

00:11:17.026 --> 00:11:19.785
until 1, 2, 3:00 in the
morning and then just

00:11:19.785 --> 00:11:22.042
start the routine all over again.

00:11:22.042 --> 00:11:24.236
And my classmates were so jealous of me

00:11:24.236 --> 00:11:26.738
that I remember like taking
my little $115 paycheck

00:11:26.738 --> 00:11:30.571
and at the time I thought
it was really a lot,

00:11:31.588 --> 00:11:35.106
and taking $115 and
trying to appease them.

00:11:35.106 --> 00:11:37.341
I would like oh, any time
you guys need any money

00:11:37.341 --> 00:11:38.926
I was always offering, oh, you need $10?

00:11:38.926 --> 00:11:41.159
Or taking them out for pizza,

00:11:41.159 --> 00:11:44.025
ordering pizza for the
class and things like that,

00:11:44.025 --> 00:11:46.545
trying to, that whole disease to please.

00:11:46.545 --> 00:11:48.089
That's where it was the
worst for me I think

00:11:48.089 --> 00:11:50.402
because I wanted to be accepted by them

00:11:50.402 --> 00:11:52.623
and could not be because first of all,

00:11:52.623 --> 00:11:53.737
I didn't have the time.

00:11:53.737 --> 00:11:55.424
They wanted me to pledge and I didn't have

00:11:55.424 --> 00:11:56.641
the time to pledge.

00:11:56.641 --> 00:11:58.555
I didn't have time to be
a part of all the other

00:11:58.555 --> 00:12:01.292
college activities or a
part of that whole lifestyle

00:12:01.292 --> 00:12:05.277
and it was very difficult for me socially.

00:12:05.277 --> 00:12:06.967
Really, one of the worst times of my life

00:12:06.967 --> 00:12:09.296
because I was trying to fit in in school

00:12:09.296 --> 00:12:10.827
and be a part of that culture,

00:12:10.827 --> 00:12:13.875
but also trying to build
a career in television.

00:12:13.875 --> 00:12:15.906
It's very difficult for
me to even see myself

00:12:15.906 --> 00:12:19.489
as successful because
I still see myself as

00:12:21.003 --> 00:12:23.518
in the process of becoming successful.

00:12:23.518 --> 00:12:26.184
To me, successful is getting to the point

00:12:26.184 --> 00:12:28.886
where you are absolutely
comfortable with yourself

00:12:28.886 --> 00:12:33.600
and it does not matter how
many things you have acquired.

00:12:33.600 --> 00:12:37.768
The ability to learn to
say no and not to feel

00:12:37.768 --> 00:12:40.102
guilty about it, to me,
is about the greatest

00:12:40.102 --> 00:12:42.050
success I have achieved.

00:12:42.050 --> 00:12:45.054
The fact that I have, you
know, in the public's eye,

00:12:45.054 --> 00:12:47.660
done whatever is fine.

00:12:47.660 --> 00:12:50.649
It's all a part of a
process for growing for me,

00:12:50.649 --> 00:12:54.018
but to me to have the
kind of internal strength

00:12:54.018 --> 00:12:57.232
and internal courage it takes to say no,

00:12:57.232 --> 00:12:58.979
I will not let you treat me this way

00:12:58.979 --> 00:13:01.332
is what success is all about.

00:13:01.332 --> 00:13:03.733
It's the same thing that
prevents you from being

00:13:03.733 --> 00:13:05.804
abused as a child, that
prevents you from being abused

00:13:05.804 --> 00:13:08.627
as an adult, that allows you
to build success for yourself.

00:13:08.627 --> 00:13:10.168
I will not be treated this way.

00:13:10.168 --> 00:13:13.012
I demand only the best for myself.

00:13:13.012 --> 00:13:15.558
You are worthy to say no.

00:13:15.558 --> 00:13:17.178
It's okay if you say no.

00:13:17.178 --> 00:13:19.982
It's okay if you say no and
then people don't like you.

00:13:19.982 --> 00:13:21.856
That's really okay.

00:13:21.856 --> 00:13:24.823
The important thing is how you
feel about what you're doing,

00:13:24.823 --> 00:13:26.936
how you feel about yourself.

00:13:26.936 --> 00:13:29.314
It's a long struggle, though.

00:13:29.314 --> 00:13:30.837
It's a long struggle.

00:13:30.837 --> 00:13:33.112
And I'm just hoping that,
you know, in the work

00:13:33.112 --> 00:13:36.143
that I do on the show and
the speaking that I do

00:13:36.143 --> 00:13:38.314
around the country and that young people

00:13:38.314 --> 00:13:40.531
who are watching this can get the lesson

00:13:40.531 --> 00:13:42.903
sooner than I did because it's painful

00:13:42.903 --> 00:13:45.140
because you keep repeating
it over and over and over

00:13:45.140 --> 00:13:47.049
until you get it right
and what I found is that

00:13:47.049 --> 00:13:50.179
every time you have to repeat
the lesson, it gets worse

00:13:50.179 --> 00:13:54.302
because I call it God trying
to get your attention,

00:13:54.302 --> 00:13:55.665
the universe trying to get your attention.

00:13:55.665 --> 00:13:57.070
So we didn't get your
attention the first time,

00:13:57.070 --> 00:13:59.383
so we're going to have to hit
you a little harder this time.

00:13:59.383 --> 00:14:01.456
So, I'm still doing
it, I'm still learning.

00:14:01.456 --> 00:14:05.289
- Create the highest,
grandest vision possible

00:14:07.552 --> 00:14:12.406
for your life because you
become what you believe.

00:14:12.406 --> 00:14:14.717
When I was a little girl, Mississippi,

00:14:14.717 --> 00:14:18.014
growing up on the farm, only
Buckwheat as a role model,

00:14:18.014 --> 00:14:22.749
watching my grandmother boil
clothes in a big iron pot

00:14:22.749 --> 00:14:24.678
through the screen door because we didn't

00:14:24.678 --> 00:14:26.895
have a washing machine and
made everything we had,

00:14:26.895 --> 00:14:30.895
I watched her and realized
somehow inside myself

00:14:32.153 --> 00:14:34.552
and the spirit of myself that although

00:14:34.552 --> 00:14:38.719
this was segregated
Mississippi and I was colored,

00:14:39.794 --> 00:14:43.814
and female, that my life could be bigger,

00:14:43.814 --> 00:14:45.814
greater than what I saw.

00:14:46.738 --> 00:14:48.450
I remember being four or five years old,

00:14:48.450 --> 00:14:50.094
I certainly couldn't articulate it,

00:14:50.094 --> 00:14:53.123
but it was a feeling and
a feeling that I allowed

00:14:53.123 --> 00:14:55.012
myself to follow.

00:14:55.012 --> 00:14:56.762
I allowed myself to follow it because

00:14:56.762 --> 00:15:00.054
if you were to ask me what
is the secret to my success,

00:15:00.054 --> 00:15:02.955
it is because I understand
that there is a power

00:15:02.955 --> 00:15:06.205
greater than myself that rules my life.

00:15:07.548 --> 00:15:09.577
(applauding)

00:15:09.577 --> 00:15:14.251
And in life, in life, if
you can be still long enough

00:15:14.251 --> 00:15:18.436
in all of your endeavors, the
good times, the hard times,

00:15:18.436 --> 00:15:22.519
to connect yourself to
the source, I call it God.

00:15:23.459 --> 00:15:25.346
You can call it whatever
you want to, the force,

00:15:25.346 --> 00:15:28.963
nature, Allah, the
power, if you can connect

00:15:28.963 --> 00:15:32.495
yourself to the source
and allow the energy

00:15:32.495 --> 00:15:35.464
that is your personality, your life force,

00:15:35.464 --> 00:15:37.355
to be connected to the greater force,

00:15:37.355 --> 00:15:39.772
anything is possible for you.

00:15:40.689 --> 00:15:42.353
I am proof of that.

00:15:42.353 --> 00:15:45.402
I think that my life and
the fact that I was born

00:15:45.402 --> 00:15:48.589
where I was born and the
time that I was and have

00:15:48.589 --> 00:15:49.808
been able to do what I've done speaks

00:15:49.808 --> 00:15:52.838
to the possibility, not that I am special,

00:15:52.838 --> 00:15:55.005
but that it could be done.

00:15:56.374 --> 00:15:59.080
I remember when I started
the school and I said

00:15:59.080 --> 00:16:01.840
to my beloved friend Maya
Angelou, I said, Maya,

00:16:01.840 --> 00:16:04.969
I'm so, I'm just so proud that I was able

00:16:04.969 --> 00:16:06.025
to create this school.

00:16:06.025 --> 00:16:07.555
I said this is going to
be my greatest legacy

00:16:07.555 --> 00:16:10.739
and Maya said to me, you have no idea.

00:16:10.739 --> 00:16:12.989
(laughing)

00:16:14.214 --> 00:16:16.332
You have no idea what your legacy will be,

00:16:16.332 --> 00:16:17.604
she said to me, because your legacy

00:16:17.604 --> 00:16:20.613
is every life you've touched.

00:16:20.613 --> 00:16:23.696
And that shifted the way I saw legacy

00:16:24.798 --> 00:16:27.344
or what you leave behind or what you do,

00:16:27.344 --> 00:16:30.856
because Maya was explaining
to me that, you know,

00:16:30.856 --> 00:16:32.666
over all the years of watching your show,

00:16:32.666 --> 00:16:34.496
everybody who decided
that they were going to

00:16:34.496 --> 00:16:36.057
go back to school or lose weight

00:16:36.057 --> 00:16:38.502
or no longer hit their children or get out

00:16:38.502 --> 00:16:40.986
of a bad marriage, all of those people

00:16:40.986 --> 00:16:44.016
who have seen and experienced your voice

00:16:44.016 --> 00:16:46.129
and the same thing with everybody here.

00:16:46.129 --> 00:16:49.664
You have no idea what your legacy will be.

00:16:49.664 --> 00:16:52.562
Your legacy is every
life that you've touched

00:16:52.562 --> 00:16:54.581
and we like to think of
it, I know you have done

00:16:54.581 --> 00:16:57.547
amazing things with your philanthropy.

00:16:57.547 --> 00:17:00.717
We like to think that these
great philanthropic moments

00:17:00.717 --> 00:17:03.923
are the ones that leave the impact

00:17:03.923 --> 00:17:06.464
or will make the huge
difference in the world,

00:17:06.464 --> 00:17:08.760
but it's really what you do every day.

00:17:08.760 --> 00:17:12.093
It's how you use your life to be a light

00:17:13.611 --> 00:17:14.709
to somebody else's.

00:17:14.709 --> 00:17:18.975
And it's how you use your
work as an expression

00:17:18.975 --> 00:17:21.011
of your own art, whatever that is.

00:17:21.011 --> 00:17:24.375
My intention in creating
master class came from

00:17:24.375 --> 00:17:27.133
the understanding that everybody's story

00:17:27.133 --> 00:17:30.836
is the same, all stories are connected

00:17:30.836 --> 00:17:35.242
and there is nothing that
anyone who's living on earth

00:17:35.242 --> 00:17:39.409
has ever felt or known or
experienced on a soul level

00:17:40.365 --> 00:17:44.038
that hasn't been felt
or known or experienced

00:17:44.038 --> 00:17:45.663
by someone else.

00:17:45.663 --> 00:17:47.434
One of the most difficult things in life

00:17:47.434 --> 00:17:50.360
is feeling that you are the only one.

00:17:50.360 --> 00:17:52.839
You are the only one
who's traveled this path,

00:17:52.839 --> 00:17:54.631
who's felt this way.

00:17:54.631 --> 00:17:55.700
- I had nowhere to go.

00:17:55.700 --> 00:17:57.772
I was homeless at the
time, I lost my family.

00:17:57.772 --> 00:18:00.902
The next thing I know, I'm
in this car for three years.

00:18:00.902 --> 00:18:02.165
Man, I'm struggling.

00:18:02.165 --> 00:18:05.818
- Who's experienced
such devastation or joy

00:18:05.818 --> 00:18:07.930
or triumph or victory.

00:18:07.930 --> 00:18:11.715
So, for me, I define a
master as someone who

00:18:11.715 --> 00:18:15.715
has fully stepped in and
owned the full progress

00:18:19.760 --> 00:18:22.042
and trajectory of their life.

00:18:22.042 --> 00:18:23.151
- Persistence pays off.

00:18:23.151 --> 00:18:24.144
That's lesson one.

00:18:24.144 --> 00:18:25.445
- But hearing stories told from the mouths

00:18:25.445 --> 00:18:29.612
of people who know how to
live, how to course correct,

00:18:30.471 --> 00:18:33.965
how to keep going, how to never quit,

00:18:33.965 --> 00:18:38.553
how to rejoice in the
good times and have faith

00:18:38.553 --> 00:18:41.053
in the bad, those people are masters.

00:18:41.053 --> 00:18:43.184
Anyone who can do that is a master

00:18:43.184 --> 00:18:45.831
and their ability to share their stories

00:18:45.831 --> 00:18:49.748
only helps the trajectory
of others who listen.

00:18:51.804 --> 00:18:53.916
What I learned, going to a beauty salon

00:18:53.916 --> 00:18:55.908
and asking them after the
news director had told

00:18:55.908 --> 00:18:58.021
me that my hair was too thick and my eyes

00:18:58.021 --> 00:18:59.565
were too far apart and I needed a makeover

00:18:59.565 --> 00:19:03.751
and sitting in a beauty salon,
in a French beauty salon,

00:19:03.751 --> 00:19:06.225
and allowing them to put a
French perm on my black hair

00:19:06.225 --> 00:19:10.392
and having the perm burn
through my cerebral cortex

00:19:11.564 --> 00:19:15.390
and not being the woman that I am now,

00:19:15.390 --> 00:19:17.746
so not having the courage
to say this is burning me

00:19:17.746 --> 00:19:22.155
and coming out a week
later bald and having

00:19:22.155 --> 00:19:26.158
to go on the air, you
learn a lot about yourself

00:19:26.158 --> 00:19:28.515
when you're black and a woman and bald

00:19:28.515 --> 00:19:30.096
and trying to be an anchorwoman.

00:19:30.096 --> 00:19:32.091
(laughing)

00:19:32.091 --> 00:19:35.424
You learn you're not Diana Ross and that

00:19:36.538 --> 00:19:39.875
you're not Barbara Walters
trying to be I was at the time.

00:19:39.875 --> 00:19:41.599
I had a lot of lessons.

00:19:41.599 --> 00:19:43.304
I remember going on the air many times

00:19:43.304 --> 00:19:45.847
and not reading my copy ahead of time

00:19:45.847 --> 00:19:48.327
and I was on the air one night

00:19:48.327 --> 00:19:51.630
and ran across the word B-A-R-B-A-D-O-S.

00:19:51.630 --> 00:19:54.747
That may be Barbados to
you, but it was Barbados

00:19:54.747 --> 00:19:56.167
to me that night.

00:19:56.167 --> 00:19:58.417
(laughing)

00:20:00.187 --> 00:20:02.874
And telling the story
as an anchorwoman about

00:20:02.874 --> 00:20:05.718
a vote in Abstentia, California.

00:20:05.718 --> 00:20:09.057
I thought it was located
near San Francisco.

00:20:09.057 --> 00:20:11.307
(laughing)

00:20:13.251 --> 00:20:15.081
And one of the worst, one of the worst,

00:20:15.081 --> 00:20:16.789
this is when I broke
out of my Barbara shell,

00:20:16.789 --> 00:20:18.205
because I'm sitting there crossing my legs

00:20:18.205 --> 00:20:20.063
trying to talk like
Barbara, be like Barbara

00:20:20.063 --> 00:20:23.432
and I was reading a story about someone

00:20:23.432 --> 00:20:25.765
with a blaze attitude, which

00:20:30.071 --> 00:20:32.104
if I had gone to Wellsley,
I would have known

00:20:32.104 --> 00:20:33.187
to was blase.

00:20:35.562 --> 00:20:37.699
And I started to laugh
at myself on the air

00:20:37.699 --> 00:20:40.787
and broke through my Barbara shell and had

00:20:40.787 --> 00:20:43.712
decided on that day
that laughing was okay,

00:20:43.712 --> 00:20:46.005
even though Barbara hadn't at that time.

00:20:46.005 --> 00:20:48.422
(applauding)

00:20:55.189 --> 00:20:56.935
And it was through my series of mistakes

00:20:56.935 --> 00:20:58.927
that I learned that I
could be a better Oprah

00:20:58.927 --> 00:21:01.255
than I could be a better
Barbara and I allowed

00:21:01.255 --> 00:21:04.597
Barbara to be the mentor for
me as she always has been

00:21:04.597 --> 00:21:08.471
and I decided then to
try to pursue the idea

00:21:08.471 --> 00:21:10.589
of being myself and I am just thrilled

00:21:10.589 --> 00:21:15.059
that I get paid so much every
day for just being myself,

00:21:15.059 --> 00:21:17.521
but it was a lesson long in coming,

00:21:17.521 --> 00:21:20.889
recognizing that I had the instinct,

00:21:20.889 --> 00:21:23.674
that the inner voice that
told me that you need

00:21:23.674 --> 00:21:27.697
to try to find a way to
answer to your own truth

00:21:27.697 --> 00:21:30.661
was the voice I needed to
be still and listen to.

00:21:30.661 --> 00:21:32.979
Get this, remember this
because this will happen

00:21:32.979 --> 00:21:34.239
many times in your life.

00:21:34.239 --> 00:21:38.239
When people show you who
they are, believe them,

00:21:39.522 --> 00:21:42.355
the first time, not the 29th time.

00:21:43.219 --> 00:21:45.681
(applauding)

00:21:45.681 --> 00:21:48.908
That's particularly good when
it comes to men situations

00:21:48.908 --> 00:21:52.725
because when he doesn't
call back the first time,

00:21:52.725 --> 00:21:56.002
when you're mistreated the first time,

00:21:56.002 --> 00:21:59.677
when you see someone who
shows you a lack of integrity

00:21:59.677 --> 00:22:03.334
or dishonesty the first
time, now that that will

00:22:03.334 --> 00:22:06.016
be followed by many,
many, many other times

00:22:06.016 --> 00:22:09.449
that will at some point in life come back

00:22:09.449 --> 00:22:11.217
to haunt or hurt you.

00:22:11.217 --> 00:22:13.267
When people show you who they are,

00:22:13.267 --> 00:22:15.809
believe them the first time.

00:22:15.809 --> 00:22:19.704
Live your life from a point
of your truth and you will.

00:22:19.704 --> 00:22:22.121
(applauding)

00:22:23.024 --> 00:22:27.670
Live your life from truth and
you will survive everything.

00:22:27.670 --> 00:22:30.761
Everything, I believe even death.

00:22:30.761 --> 00:22:34.600
You will survive everything
if you can live your life

00:22:34.600 --> 00:22:36.596
from a point of view of truth.

00:22:36.596 --> 00:22:40.700
Close your eyes for a
moment will you please.

00:22:40.700 --> 00:22:42.199
And breathe with me.

00:22:42.199 --> 00:22:43.545
Just close your eyes and if you will

00:22:43.545 --> 00:22:47.462
put your thumb to your
middle finger and gather

00:22:50.777 --> 00:22:54.837
your other fingers around
and let's feel the vibration

00:22:54.837 --> 00:22:58.186
and pulse of your personal
energy as you take

00:22:58.186 --> 00:23:00.436
three deep breaths with me.

00:23:02.295 --> 00:23:03.128
Inhale.

00:23:08.088 --> 00:23:12.255
And as you exhale, just
feel the vibration, energy,

00:23:16.273 --> 00:23:20.190
blood pulsating through
your body, through you.

00:23:23.054 --> 00:23:24.637
And another inhale.

00:23:36.980 --> 00:23:38.563
And another inhale.

00:23:46.582 --> 00:23:48.749
And keep your eyes closed.

00:23:51.806 --> 00:23:54.806
And let's just think about this day.

00:24:01.785 --> 00:24:05.618
This day that you have
been graced to breathe.

00:24:08.066 --> 00:24:08.983
In and out.

00:24:10.318 --> 00:24:11.901
Thousands of times.

00:24:15.578 --> 00:24:18.239
This day, where many of those breaths

00:24:18.239 --> 00:24:19.948
were taken for granted.

00:24:19.948 --> 00:24:23.198
You just expected the next one to come.

00:24:24.354 --> 00:24:25.678
But the truth is there is no guarantee

00:24:25.678 --> 00:24:27.678
that the next one comes.

00:24:29.111 --> 00:24:32.731
This day, how you started your day,

00:24:32.731 --> 00:24:35.814
what your thoughts were this morning,

00:24:38.474 --> 00:24:42.224
how you've carried
yourself through this day.

00:24:44.597 --> 00:24:47.824
How you've been allowed to have encounters

00:24:47.824 --> 00:24:50.657
and experiences, some challenging,

00:24:52.534 --> 00:24:54.617
some more life enhancing.

00:24:58.226 --> 00:25:02.309
That pushed you forward
another day of being here

00:25:04.180 --> 00:25:07.263
on the planet earth as a human being.

00:25:10.619 --> 00:25:12.716
Let's just think about that,

00:25:12.716 --> 00:25:16.716
after all you've been
through in this day alone,

00:25:21.204 --> 00:25:24.121
and the many days and years passed,

00:25:26.382 --> 00:25:30.549
how you got here to this
prestigious esteemed university,

00:25:33.010 --> 00:25:37.177
the choices you made that
have brought you to this day.

00:25:42.803 --> 00:25:46.053
Open your heart and quietly to yourself

00:25:51.458 --> 00:25:55.625
say the only prayer that's
ever needed, thank you.

00:26:02.064 --> 00:26:02.897
Thank you.

00:26:05.866 --> 00:26:06.699
Thank you.

00:26:10.011 --> 00:26:11.511
You're still here.

00:26:12.828 --> 00:26:15.911
And you get another chance, this day,

00:26:18.910 --> 00:26:22.788
to do better and be better, another chance

00:26:22.788 --> 00:26:25.955
to become more of who you were created

00:26:32.090 --> 00:26:35.222
and what you were created to fulfill.

00:26:35.222 --> 00:26:36.055
Thank you.

00:26:39.204 --> 00:26:40.361
- Thank you guys so much for watching.

00:26:40.361 --> 00:26:43.715
I made this video because
Charlene Benton asked me to.

00:26:43.715 --> 00:26:45.381
If there's someone
you'd like me to profile

00:26:45.381 --> 00:26:47.654
in our future Top 10,
please check out the link

00:26:47.654 --> 00:26:49.260
down in the description below
and you can cast your vote

00:26:49.260 --> 00:26:52.045
on who we should do next.

00:26:52.045 --> 00:26:53.856
I also want to give a quick
shout-out to Megan Lofton.

00:26:53.856 --> 00:26:55.926
Megan, thank you so much for picking up

00:26:55.926 --> 00:26:58.424
a copy of my book Your One
Word and doing the review

00:26:58.424 --> 00:27:00.236
and posting it on the
YouTube channel as well.

00:27:00.236 --> 00:27:02.239
I really, really, really
appreciate the support

00:27:02.239 --> 00:27:05.322
and I'm so glad you enjoyed the book.

00:27:06.917 --> 00:27:07.933
Thank you guys again for watching.

00:27:07.933 --> 00:27:09.024
I believe in you.

00:27:09.024 --> 00:27:10.412
I hope you continue to believe in yourself

00:27:10.412 --> 00:27:12.525
and whatever your one word is, much love.

00:27:12.525 --> 00:27:14.025
I'll see you soon.

00:27:21.221 --> 00:27:24.588
- I have paid attention to my life

00:27:24.588 --> 00:27:27.972
because I understand that
my life just like your life

00:27:27.972 --> 00:27:32.134
is always speaking to you where you are,

00:27:32.134 --> 00:27:36.301
in the language, with the
people, with the circumstances

00:27:37.213 --> 00:27:40.732
and experiences that you
can understand and interpret

00:27:40.732 --> 00:27:44.732
if you are willing to see
that always life, God,

00:27:49.589 --> 00:27:51.962
is speaking to you.

00:27:51.962 --> 00:27:55.905
Now it took me a while to
actually really get this

00:27:55.905 --> 00:27:57.815
and to understand it, but once I did,

00:27:57.815 --> 00:28:01.228
I started paying attention to everything

00:28:01.228 --> 00:28:05.351
and one of the reasons
why I can now accept

00:28:05.351 --> 00:28:09.518
the fact that I can offer
my gatherings of information

00:28:11.857 --> 00:28:14.638
and wisdom and call
myself a spiritual teacher

00:28:14.638 --> 00:28:18.643
is that every single person
who ever came on my show

00:28:18.643 --> 00:28:23.398
and I hear there was like
37,000 guests I've talked to,

00:28:23.398 --> 00:28:26.242
a lot of them came from dysfunction

00:28:26.242 --> 00:28:28.636
and a lot of them wouldn't
appear to be teachers,

00:28:28.636 --> 00:28:30.752
but every one of them had something to say

00:28:30.752 --> 00:28:33.479
that was meaningful and valuable

00:28:33.479 --> 00:28:36.734
and that I could use to grow myself

00:28:36.734 --> 00:28:39.901
into the best of myself, which is what

00:28:40.980 --> 00:28:43.151
all of our jobs are.

00:28:43.151 --> 00:28:47.175
Your number one job is to
become more of yourself

00:28:47.175 --> 00:28:50.713
and to grow yourself into
the best of yourself.

00:28:50.713 --> 00:28:53.215
- [Interviewer] How have you
start fresh and how have you,

00:28:53.215 --> 00:28:55.508
what can you attribute staying
in the biz for so long?

00:28:55.508 --> 00:28:58.149
I think every you're
trying to reinvent yourself

00:28:58.149 --> 00:29:01.057
and you're staying in touch
with what other people

00:29:01.057 --> 00:29:02.926
are doing, thinking, feeling.

00:29:02.926 --> 00:29:07.044
I have always felt that
my instinct and ability

00:29:07.044 --> 00:29:09.425
to connect with the audience was what

00:29:09.425 --> 00:29:11.292
carries us every day.

00:29:11.292 --> 00:29:13.166
Every day after the
show now I do something

00:29:13.166 --> 00:29:14.503
called After the Show,
which airs on Oxygen,

00:29:14.503 --> 00:29:17.729
I have spent for the past
16 years half an hour,

00:29:17.729 --> 00:29:21.479
an hour just talking to
people so my audience

00:29:24.440 --> 00:29:26.617
comes from a cross section
around the country,

00:29:26.617 --> 00:29:28.689
so I stay connected to
what people are thinking

00:29:28.689 --> 00:29:31.452
and doing and want and so forth.

00:29:31.452 --> 00:29:34.312
As I've grown older, I've
learned to appreciate

00:29:34.312 --> 00:29:38.235
living in the moment and
I ask that you to, too.

00:29:38.235 --> 00:29:41.913
I'm asking this graduating
class, those of you here,

00:29:41.913 --> 00:29:44.838
I've asked all of my viewers in America

00:29:44.838 --> 00:29:47.724
and across the world to do this one thing.

00:29:47.724 --> 00:29:49.958
Keep a grateful journal.

00:29:49.958 --> 00:29:54.753
Every night list five things
that happened this day

00:29:54.753 --> 00:29:58.336
and days to come that
you are grateful for.

00:29:59.242 --> 00:30:02.190
What it will begin to do is
to change your perspective

00:30:02.190 --> 00:30:04.357
of your day and your life.

00:30:05.461 --> 00:30:07.658
I believe that if you
can learn to focus on

00:30:07.658 --> 00:30:10.678
what you have, you will
always see that the universe

00:30:10.678 --> 00:30:13.608
is abundant and you will have more.

00:30:13.608 --> 00:30:16.818
If you concentrate and focus in your life

00:30:16.818 --> 00:30:18.706
on what you don't have,
you will never have enough.

00:30:18.706 --> 00:30:20.800
Be grateful, keep a journal.

00:30:20.800 --> 00:30:24.217
You all are all over my journal tonight.

